WEBVTT

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:03.420
<i>I'm here, America!</i>

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:14.200
<i>The land where baseball was born...</i>

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:17.660
<i>The last time I came here...</i>

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.690
<i>I was just overwhelmed by the scale of things, but...</i>

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.510
<i>this time...</i>

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:26.910
<i>I can compete with this country using my own strength!</i>

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.330
I can't go home empty-handed!

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.660
Oh! I'm sorry!

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.160
Are you okay?

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.460
I'm so sorry.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.000
I'll wipe it up right away.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.540
Eh, well...

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:52.700
Is this okay?

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.560
O-Okay, okay... Yes, yes!

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:57.470
Bye!

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.230
Bye!!

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:06.390
I can't believe she's the same species as Shimizu!

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.070
Hurray for America! 

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.070
Hurray!

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:15.940
I-It's gone!

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:16.770
I-It's gone!

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:17.620
My bag's gone!

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:23.930
<i>I-I've been deceived!</i>

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.380
<i>I-I've been deceived!</i>

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.590
Hey, wait! You!

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:31.060
That bag just has things like my glove and my change of clothes!

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:33.700
There's no point in stealing those!

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.830
I'm done for.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:42.500
My card, my money, the airplane ticket for tomorrow:

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:43.360
My card, my money, the airplane ticket for tomorrow:

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.340
My card, my money, the airplane ticket for tomorrow:

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.250
They've all been taken.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.410
Having my luggage stolen so quickly after arriving...

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.500
It's too embarrassing; I can't call home.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:10.050
All I've got left is the 20 dollar bill that I had in my socks,

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:12.180
a guidebook, and my passport.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:13.560
Damn!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.860
I was going to stay here overnight...

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:20.890
and fly to Arizona where the tryouts are first thing tomorrow!

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.550
<i>Be careful!</i>

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:29.150
<i>Especially in airports, incidents of people stealing luggage is common.</i>

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.490
<i>Like I'd do something so clumsy.</i>

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:40.660
In the end, I'd rather die than call home for help!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.790
No use just sitting around brooding over this!

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.220
Since it's come to this, I'll just have to do something on my own!

00:03:58.870 --> 00:03:59.850
Damn!

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:03.010
Arizona is 600 km away.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.360
Hey, someone, please stop!

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.770
Damn it!

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.860
Americans sure are cold!

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:17.330
Won't anybody give this poor Japanese boy a ride!?

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.010
I-It stopped!

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.280
I-It stopped!

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.540
T-Thank you! Thank you!

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:31.010
I love Arizona, please, please!

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.800
A Japanese person?

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.140
Hey, you, what are you doing in this kind of place?

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.800
What do you mean, "what"? I'm hitchhiking!

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.360
For the time being, I need to go to Arizona!

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:49.080
It's all right if you leave me somewhere along the road, so will you give me a ride?

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.070
I didn't stop to give you a ride.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.530
Hitchhiking is supposed to be prohibited in most states.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.980
Even if you try to hitchhike, since the crime rate is so high in America,

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.490
no one would stop to pick you up.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:03.490
R-Really?

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.030
You'll have to figure out another way to get there.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:06.770
Bye.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:08.510
Hey!

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.370
Then give me a ride!

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.420
Aren't we both Japanese?

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.790
Hey!

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:24.160
I don't care if it's prohibited or anything,

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:27.090
but I don't have any money, so I have no choice other than to hitchhike!

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.750
That taco-head!

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.770
Well, if I just get to Arizona...

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:35.490
and get them to admit my strength,

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.770
I won't just be getting a contract,

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.940
they'll probably give me a VIP welcoming!

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.360
Police!?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.540
Hey, you, what are you doing here?

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:52.460
Hitchhiking is prohibited!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:53.710
W-What!?

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:54.960
W-What!?

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:56.780
No hitchhike!

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:57.700
Okay?

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.410
Y-Yes!

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:01.280
Okay, okay!

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:04.720
Even if I say that,{Lloyd: I'm not sure the first sound is part of the sentence... so please check}

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.780
with just 20 dollars,

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:10.200
I can't get to Arizona through conventional means.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:14.320
There's no choice.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:18.320
I'll have to swallow my pride and plead on my knees to my family.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.420
You!

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:33.350
You bastard! How dare you do what you did!

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.340
Where in Arizona?

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.550
Travelling five hours alone is boring after all.

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:40.960
I'll give you a ride as far as Phoenix.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:46.980
I'm saved!

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:50.680
To be given a ride all the way to Phoenix, my destination, immediately...

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.350
It's like a dream!

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.720
You're a nice guy!

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.610
Shigeno, was it?

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.300
What's your business in Phoenix?

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.780
If you're going sightseeing, then Hollywood or Las Vegas would be better choices.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:03.530
Sightseeing?

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:07.750
Like I'd spend ten hours flying here on a plane for that.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:11.460
It's baseball.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.400
I played baseball straight through high school.

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:18.400
Well, it's been a road of many choices though.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:24.300
For the time being I'm going to take a shot at challenging the most interesting one, the Major League.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.270
The enrollment test for that...

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:30.060
is being conducted in a camp by a baseball team in Arizona.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:31.020
Oh?

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.470
By the way,

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.160
what's your name?

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.440
Are you here on a trip from Japan?

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:40.360
I'm Yaginuma Hayato.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:43.050
I studied three years at Kanto University and am 21 years old.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:44.530
I throw right-handed, hit right-handed,

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.270
and my position is shortstop.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:49.160
When I was in high school, I also went to Koshien.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:53.300
Koshien, huh?

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:57.640
Huh? W-What!?

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.000
You're slow.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:10.850
Is just water really enough?

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:15.120
Yes, yes, I love water, you see.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.930
You're sure you're not going to eat?

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.740
You haven't eaten anything after the in-flight meal, right?

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:26.140
W-Well, I've got no appetite.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:31.790
<i>It's because I don't have any money that I'm hitchhiking, you know.</i>

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:34.550
But, really,

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:39.530
to think that there would be another Japanese person other than me who would try out for the Majors...

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:43.720
Right now, that's one route if you're aspiring to play baseball in America.

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:45.220
It's not rare.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:46.660
Or...

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:51.470
did you delude yourself into thinking you were special?

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:56.350
Well, even with that, it's not something you can easily achieve.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:08:59.880
As for me...

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:02.650
I took the test three times last year, but...

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:03.860
I didn't make it.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:05.460
Last year too?

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:09.530
My parents opposed it and wanted me to get a job.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.240
I thought that...

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:15.250
if I could just get a Minor League contract during my enrollment in university,

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:17.500
I'd be able to convince them, but...

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.650
Even so, this year is my last chance.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:22.870
If I can't do it during this trip to the States,

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:25.330
I'll have to search for a job for real next year.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:28.110
What!?

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.900
What's so funny?

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:30.930
Nothing.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:33.600
You love baseball too.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:36.880
Neither of us know what will happen, but...

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:40.280
let's dream a beautiful dream while we can and do our best!

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:44.970
That's true.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:47.200
Then, is it okay if I eat this potato?

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.800
What do you mean by "then"?

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:08.280
Oh, you've woken up, Ginumacchi.

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:10.190
Where have you been?

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:13.960
Well, even if you went out of your way to get a twin room,

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.140
I could hardly sleep because of the time difference.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.580
I ran around the area a bit.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:21.870
Even back in Japan, if I didn't do my routine of running 20 kilometers every morning and evening,

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.110
I wouldn't be able to relax.

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.070
20 kilometers?

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:27.030
I'm going to borrow the shower for a bit.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:34.940
Which team are you trying out for?

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:37.770
Um, which one was it again?

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:40.390
I think it was the "something Salmons."

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.590
"I think it was something"... What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:45.220
It can't be helped, can it?

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.050
Since the notebook I wrote it down in, among other things,

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:48.840
has been stolen.

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:51.020
Most likely,

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:52.960
it's the Anaheim Salmons.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.390
That's where I'm going today too.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:11:00.480
What? You're trying out for the Salmons too?

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:01.780
Yeah.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:04.050
I'm trying out as a fielder though.

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.650
How are you going to get a glove and cleats?

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:08.410
Well, I'll borrow them from someone.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:09.930
As long as my body's unharmed...

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:11.820
I can stand on the mound.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:16.160
Shigeno.

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:20.120
Before the test, would you mind doing a little warmup?

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.960
Show me your pitching.

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:34.300
Wouldn't it be best if we stopped now?

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:37.890
What do you mean?

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.130
Have you ever played catcher?

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.730
You'll get hurt with an infielder's glove.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.450
Don't make fun of me!

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:47.370
I'm not that bad!

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:47.370
Hey!

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.080
Playing catch is prohibited here.

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:52.160
What are you going to do if you hit one of the guests' cars?

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.770
Sorry.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:55.920
What is it?

00:11:56.490 --> 00:11:58.740
He told us not to play catch here.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:01.920
What? I just got my shoulder warmed up.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.080
Hey, please!

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.040
Last one only, okay?

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.390
Oh, all right.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.260
Just one more throw.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:14.540
He said that you can throw one final pitch, Shigeno.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:17.180
Okay, okay! Thank you, old man!

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:19.250
Well, with that glove...

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:21.600
you won't want to catch a second pitch anyway.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:25.560
<i>Running 20 kilometers every morning and evening...</i>

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:28.980
<i>and that hardened physique...</i>

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:30.610
<i>This guy...</i>

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:32.440
<i>It seems like he went to a common high school, but...</i>

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:35.440
<i>just how fast can he pitch?</i>

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.330
<i>Make sure you don't hurt yourself...</i>

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:40.200
<i>right before the test!</i>

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:51.510
NO!!!

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:54.220
I'm surprised.

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:55.410
If nothing else,

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:57.770
at least your speed is at the Major League level.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:58.810
With that pitch,

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.850
why couldn't you go to Koshien?

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:02.770
Don't know.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:06.550
If I was skillful enough to go to Koshien,

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.760
I wouldn't be in this kind of place right now.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:14.740
Well, no skilled person would get their luggage stolen, after all.

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:15.840
That's true.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.820
Hey! Shut up!

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:22.870
This is a free fansub.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:22.870
Not for sale or rent.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:25.270
Oh, come on!

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:26.790
What is he doing?

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:30.150
He said he'd call as soon as he got to the hotel!

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:31.750
It's been two days since he departed from Japan!

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:34.800
Geez! That boy always makes me worry!

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:35.690
Hey!

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:37.290
Calm down.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.250
Sooner or later, he'll contact us.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.680
But...

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:42.220
Hey!

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:43.430
Goro-oniichan...

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:46.220
You think he's become a Major Leaguer?

00:13:47.230 --> 00:13:48.690
I'm sure he has.

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:50.530
I know that...

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:56.110
only the best Japanese pros can become a Major Leaguer!

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.900
To be able to go to such a place...

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.250
Goro-oniichan...

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.040
sure is great!

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:06.150
But to become a Major Leaguer...

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:08.480
he'll have to pass the test.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:10.750
Hey, hey, wait a minute!

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:13.050
It's not that simple.

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:14.910
It isn't?

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.260
Listen,

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:18.420
under each baseball team of the Major League...

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:22.220
there exists a system called the Minor League.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.490
The Minor Leagues are divided into:

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:25.620
Triple A,

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:26.640
Double A,

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:27.860
Single A,

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:29.150
and the Rookie League...

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:30.980
depending on their level.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:35.000
In each and every one, lots of people try to enroll.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.190
Purple?

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:37.110
Double?

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:41.590
In other words, if you compared it to Japanese Professional Baseball,

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:46.610
under the first team is the second, third, fourth, fifth, and many more.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:49.250
Everyone aims for the first team.

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:53.000
Then that will lead to fights, right?

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:54.920
That's right.

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:58.720
In all of America, the amount of players associated with the Minor League is...

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:00.780
over 5000 people, after all.

00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:02.390
That many?

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.900
Even if you pass the tryout,

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:09.260
you'll have to start at the lowest level: the Rookie League.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:13.380
If you can win and remain in that competition, you'll go up one level.

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:16.520
Then you'll have to fight to remain and move upwards again.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:19.890
Competing with 5000 rivals,

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:23.490
having climbed up the pyramid from the base to the summit...

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:26.620
are a handful of superstars.

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:28.140
That's...

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:29.740
a Major Leaguer.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.440
Oh! Here they are!

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:34.990
Young men with big dreams!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.280
Hey, Shigeno.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.340
We'll go to the reception desk first.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:47.220
Shortstop, Yaginuma, and pitcher, Shigeno, is it?

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:50.030
Doesn't seem like you've got letters of recommendation, but...

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:51.270
going to give it a try?

00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:53.050
Yes, we will.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.390
Okay.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.350
We'll call out to you when it's your turn.

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:57.780
Warm up and wait.

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:00.150
Excuse me...

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:04.570
I am no glove and spike shoes.

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:07.070
Rental! Rental, please!

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:07.740
What?

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.990
Please! Please!

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:11.160
No, you idiot!

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:14.340
Go home!

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:17.040
You're not worthy of taking our test!

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:21.110
What did this old man just say?

00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:21.930
Come here for a minute!

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:22.560
W-What is it?

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.010
W-What is it?

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:27.030
You fool!

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:29.220
What kind of idiot would say that kind of thing?

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:30.680
W-What do you mean?

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.550
Everyone is taking this test seriously.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.220
Naturally, someone who hasn't even brought his equipment...

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.610
will be sent home immediately!

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:40.970
This isn't the time to just say "Ah."

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.030
Geez...

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:43.270
Yaginuma!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.530
You'll start with running 60 yards.

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:48.460
Go to the far left zone.

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:49.450
Yes, sir!

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:51.060
Anyway,

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:53.020
I won't look after you anymore!

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:54.540
After you've apologized, borrow what you need from someone.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:56.490
Deal with this by yourself!

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.510
This is bad...

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.230
Even if I'm told to borrow from someone,

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:07.890
everyone's eyes are focused.

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:10.310
It's not an atmosphere where you can just go up to people and talk.

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:13.720
Sorry!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.260
Please throw it back!{yes I know this is a long lead-in, but I don't like it blinking either}

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:23.390
Hey!

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:24.280
Come on!

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:37.870
Huh?

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:40.000
Damn!

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:43.160
And I was going to show off too!

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:45.590
If I had cleats, I wouldn't have slipped!

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.110
<i>That form...</i>

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:48.940
<i>No...</i>

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:51.510
<i>Even while slipping, that speed...</i>

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.450
Can't be helped!

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.730
When Ginumacchi is done, I'll borrow his cleats.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:58.260
Hey, you.

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:02.400
What's your shoe size?

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:12.890
The harvest this year is really poor.

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:13.930
Yeah.

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:17.400
There are too many people who aren't even at the Minor League level.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:18.210
Next!

00:18:26.110 --> 00:18:27.250
H-Hey!

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:28.530
Wait a minute!

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:31.880
Who are you, daring to take the test in jeans!?

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.150
Sorry, Steve.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.950
I gave him permission.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:38.270
If he sucks, you can disqualify him after just one pitch.

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:40.190
Please watch.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:43.200
Okay!

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:44.820
Go ahead and throw.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:47.240
Shigeno?

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:51.660
<i>Thanks, old man!</i>

00:18:52.010 --> 00:18:55.280
<i>Unless your blue eyes are only knotholes,</i>

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:58.620
<i>I won't disappoint you!</i>

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:16.530
How many miles per hour was it?

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:18.450
N-Ninety-nine miles per hour!

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:20.100
N-Ninety-nine miles per hour!

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:24.480
Who is this Asian?

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:26.700
<i>99 mph?</i>

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.190
<i>That's 159 km/h!</i>

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:31.990
Scott!

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:32.930
Yes?

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:35.780
Go fetch Bolton from the Main Ground!

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:50.100
<i>I damaged my foot half a year ago.</i>

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.250
<i>Without rushing,</i>

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.720
<i>I took my time and...</i>

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:55.570
<i>carefully did numerous rehabilitation exercises...</i>

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.390
<i>waiting for this day!</i>

00:19:58.510 --> 00:19:59.930
<i>I've always been able to hear it.</i>

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:05.790
<i>The scream coming from my body,</i>

00:20:05.790 --> 00:20:09.110
<i>crying to play baseball!</i>

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.020
I'm shocked.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:13.440
His control is really good too!

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:14.030
Okay!

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:16.480
Next, throw a breaking ball!

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:18.140
Breaking ball?

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:21.500
Oh, a henka kyuu, huh?

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:25.290
I am...

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.120
fastball only!

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:29.840
This is my policy! Okay?

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.900
Just a fastball?

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:33.760
Oh?

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:37.470
Quite a lively Asian, it seems.

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:38.690
Bolton!

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:40.390
So you came.

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.090
B-Bolton?

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.730
Why are you here?

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:46.770
I called for him.

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:51.980
Don't you want to see how well Shigeno's stuff will work against a Major League slugger?

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.500
B-But...

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:55.490
To call our cleanup hitter for such a thing...

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:57.250
I don't mind.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:58.660
It's an interesting show.

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.470
I was bored with simply...

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:03.870
weight training just now.

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:05.380
Oh?

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:07.150
I don't know who that is, but...

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:10.340
with that body build, he doesn't seem like an ordinary person.

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:11.870
<i>I-I can't believe this!</i>

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.610
<i>I-I can't believe this!</i>

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:16.110
<i>That they would send for a Major Leaguer all of a sudden...</i>

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:17.510
<i>That Shigeno...</i>

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.350
Come on, boy.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:31.980
<i>I thought the probability that I'd have to start in the Minor League was high, but...</i>

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:34.820
<i>it doesn't seem like I'll have to take a detour.</i>

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:35.980
<i>Right now,</i>

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:38.450
<i>I'll grasp the Majors with this hand!</i>

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:42.190
S-Strike!

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:43.330
S-Strike!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.180
<i>I see...</i>

00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:51.790
<i>I understand why they called me out, even though it's only a tryout.</i>

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:53.130
<i>This is unbearable!</i>

00:21:53.130 --> 00:21:55.300
<i>This excitement surpasses what I usually get from a test!</i>

00:21:57.610 --> 00:21:59.300
Strike two!

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:02.250
You're cornered.

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:04.970
Can you get the timing right on the last ball without having swung?

00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:11.650
<i>You're too busy thinking up an excuse...</i>

00:22:11.650 --> 00:22:12.860
<i>for when you've been struck out, huh!?</i>

00:22:30.020 --> 00:22:31.900
The American Dream...

00:22:31.900 --> 00:22:35.380
isn't that easy, Asian rookie!

00:24:11.640 --> 00:24:13.510
My pitch has been hit right off the bat!

00:24:13.510 --> 00:24:15.310
Just what I'd expect from a Major Leaguer!

00:24:15.310 --> 00:24:16.610
If it wasn't this way,

00:24:16.610 --> 00:24:18.980
there wouldn't have been any meaning in coming to America!

00:24:19.530 --> 00:24:21.190
Next time, on Major:

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:22.390
Tryouts.

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:25.220
Run to the stage of your dreams!
